--- (2) THE PREDICTION'S QUANTITATIVE FORM: f_pair/f_LCDM = (1 + r_M/s)^q ---
       THE DERIVATION (registered, closed form):
       (a) the disruption (Roche-class) criterion with the 1/r force: the
           satellite at separation s is disrupted when the host's tidal field
           at its edge matches its self-binding there; the classical boundary
           (the tidal radius) is r_t = s (M_sat/M_host)^(1/3)-class.
       (b) the deep-regime force ratio at the satellite's edge -- the ratio of
           the tidally-relevant field to the baryon-only one -- is
           eta(s) = 1 + r_M/s  [r_M = r_M(pair) at the matched-pair anchor;
           = 2.000 exactly at s = r_M, the pair-scale equipartition, G086's
           anchor; at the satellite scale: eta = 1 + r_M,sat/s, r_M,sat =
           sqrt(G M_sat/a0) -- the (1 + r_M,sat/s)-class of the brief].
       (c) the criterion's boundary is SCALED BY this force ratio (first
           power), and the surviving-pair population at fixed stellar mass
           responds to the boundary LINEARLY -> q = 1, the closed form:
               f_pair(s) / f_pair,LCDM(s) = (1 + r_M(s)/s)^1
         s = r_M/2 : eta = 3.000  excess factor =   3.000  (+200.0%)
         s = r_M   : eta = 2.000  excess factor =   2.000  (+100.0%)
         s = 2 r_M : eta = 1.500  excess factor =   1.500  (+ 50.0%)
       the log-slope of the excess vs separation at the anchor:
