--- THE FALSIFIERS (pre-registered; any one kills) ---
  F1 [the anchor] f_pair(s) at or BELOW the LCDM expectation at s ~ r_M (the
     anchor bin s/r_M in [2/3, 4/3]: excess ratio <= 1.00) kills the prediction --
     the registered +100% at the pair-scale equipartition is the core statement.
  F2 [the slope] a measured excess that does NOT follow (1 + r_M/s)^q: the slope
     q_meas = d log10(excess)/d log10(1 + r_M/s) outside [0.5, 1.5] -- including
     q_meas <= 0 (flat or falling toward small s), i.e. a RISING f_pair(s) with
     the WRONG slope (the q) -- kills; the G086-literal axis (1 + s/r_M) sits at
     3.000 at 2 r_M vs the registered 1.500: the 2 r_M bin discriminates the axes.
  F3 [the M_b-only statement] the excess that scales with halo concentration or
     environment instead of (1 + r_M/s) with r_M from M_b alone kills -- the
     universal-curve test: the excess over stellar-mass bins must collapse onto
     the single curve in s/r_M (scatter < the pre-registered 20%).
  F4 [the window] an excess confined OUTSIDE the registered window (e.g. only
     s < r_M/2, or only at the survey's projected-fringe scales) kills the
     registered curve (the window-integrated median excess ~ 1.5 is the prior).

